// Korean pyeongsang: low wooden platform in the village square, about 4.0 x 3.0 blocks, ~0.95 high
// Parts (1 block = 1 m):
//  - spruce deck top: 8 planks, each 0.43 wide, 0.14 thick, with gaps
//  - two front/back beams and a middle beam under the deck
//  - 8 stripped spruce posts down to the ground
//  - hay straw mat (3.5 x 2.7) with a darker border and weave lines
//  - low table 0.8 x 0.6 x 0.3 high on the mat, with 4 legs, cups, a teapot and a small lamp
// Front faces -Z, toward the player. Centre x = 0, deck spans z 0.8 to 3.8.

def cz = 2.3          // centre of platform along z
def hw = 2.0          // half width (x)
def hd = 1.5          // half depth (z)
def deckTop = 0.95
def deckBot = 0.81

// deck boards running front to back
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    double bx = -hw + i * 0.51
